  "abstract": "<p>\n                    In this paper, bounds given in the first part of the paper are strengthened. In addition, it is shown that the interval\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left-parenthesis x comma x plus x slash 16597 right-parenthesis\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>+</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mrow class=\"MJX-TeXAtom-ORD\">\n                              <mml:mo>/</mml:mo>\n                            </mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mn>16597</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mml:mo>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">(x,x + x/16597)</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    contains a prime for all\n                    <inline-formula content-type=\"math/mathml\">\n                      <mml:math xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x greater-than-or-slanted-equals 2 comma 010 comma 760\">\n                        <mml:semantics>\n                          <mml:mrow>\n                            <mml:mi>x</mml:mi>\n                            <mml:mo>\n                              ⩾\n                              \n                            </mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>2</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>010</mml:mn>\n                            <mml:mo>,</mml:mo>\n                            <mml:mn>760</mml:mn>\n                          </mml:mrow>\n                          <mml:annotation encoding=\"application/x-tex\">x \\geqslant 2,010,760</mml:annotation>\n                        </mml:semantics>\n                      </mml:math>\n                    </inline-formula>\n                    ; and explicit bounds for the Chebyshev functions are given under the assumption of the Riemann hypothesis.\n                  </p>",
